  "uncertain": [
    "Label choice: each pad has a level-1 pin name (e.g. PB_12) and a GPIO-style name (e.g. GPIOPB_12) inside the multiplexed list; the pin name was used as label.",
    "Mapping of the multiplexed-function boxes to pads relies on crossing leader lines (left side); the GPIOPx_n suffixes agree with the pin names except PA_5, whose box reads GPIOPB_5."
  ],
  "notes": "W600 WiFi Module v1.01 pinout. Per the image note: first level = pin name (used as label), second level = default function, third level = multiplexed functions (split on '/' except inside 'SPI(M/S)'). Module silkscreen spellings put first in functions when different. Printed text copied as shown, including 'GPIOPB_5' on the PA_5 pad and 'SPI(M/S)_D1' on PB_17."
